{"causes":["Anne was forced into hiding by the Nazis in 1942 after her father's business was discovered as Jewish.","The Nazi occupation of the Netherlands led to widespread persecution and violence against Jews.","World War II created a global context in which millions were displaced, killed, or forced into hiding."],"effects":["The Diary of Anne Frank has become a symbol of hope and resilience for millions worldwide.","It has inspired numerous adaptations, interpretations, and scholarly analyses, cementing its place in the annals of modern history.","Its legacy continues to educate and raise awareness about the Holocaust and its consequences."],"relationships":[{"sourceSlug":"archbishop-ussher","sourceName":"Archbishop Ussher","verb":"CONTAINS","targetSlug":"diary-of-anne-frank","targetName":"Diary of Anne Frank","context":"Ussher's 1650 Annales Veteris Testamenti is a historical work that predates the Diary of Anne Frank."},{"sourceSlug":"nazi-occupation","sourceName":"Nazi Occupation","verb":"OCCURS_DURING","targetSlug":"diary-of-anne-frank","targetName":"Diary of Anne Frank","context":"The diary chronicles the Franks' experiences during the Nazi occupation of the Netherlands."},{"sourceSlug":"holocaust","sourceName":"Holocaust","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"diary-of-anne-frank","targetName":"Diary of Anne Frank","context":"The diary is a primary source documenting the daily experiences of Jews during the Holocaust."},{"sourceSlug":"Anne-Frank-Museum","sourceName":"Anne Frank Museum","verb":"CONTAINS","targetSlug":"diary-of-anne-frank","targetName":"Diary of Anne Frank","context":"The museum houses a collection of artifacts and exhibits related to the diary."},{"sourceSlug":"amsterdam","sourceName":"Amsterdam","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"diary-of-anne-frank","targetName":"Diary of Anne Frank","context":"The Franks lived in secret in Amsterdam during their time in hiding."},{"sourceSlug":"museum-quay-Amsterdam","sourceName":"Museumquay Amsterdam","verb":"CONTAINS","targetSlug":"diary-of-anne-frank","targetName":"Diary of Anne Frank","context":"The museum was built on the site where the Franks lived in hiding."},{"sourceSlug":"anne-frank-trust","sourceName":"Anne Frank Trust","verb":"PARTICIPATES_IN","targetSlug":"diary-of-anne-frank","targetName":"Diary of Anne Frank","context":"The trust manages the rights to the diary and its legacy."},{"sourceSlug":"jewish-resistance-movement","sourceName":"Jewish Resistance Movement","verb":"COLLABORATES_WITH","targetSlug":"diary-of-anne-frank","targetName":"Diary of Anne Frank","context":"The movement supported the Franks during their time in hiding."},{"sourceSlug":"Anne-Frank-Society","sourceName":"Anne Frank Society","verb":"PARTICIPATES_IN","targetSlug":"diary-of-anne-frank","targetName":"Diary of Anne Frank","context":"The society promotes education and awareness about the diary's significance."}],"places":[{"name":"Amsterdam","role":"Birthplace"},{"name":"Museumquay Amsterdam","role":"Major battle"},{"name":"Nazi Germany","role":"Occupation"}],"texts":[{"title":"Wikipedia: Diary of Anne Frank","type":"Reference article","slug":"diary-of-anne-frank"}],"externalLinks":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q6911","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Diary_of_a_Young_Girl"],"tags":["literary work","Historical & Literary Texts","cause-and-effect"],"thumbnailUrl":"","quote":"","legacySummary":"Diary of Anne Frank left a notable mark on Modern history, documented across 80 Wikipedia editions worldwide. Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.","summary":"The Diary of a Young Girl (Dutch: Het Achterhuis, 'The Secret Annex'), commonly known as The Diary of Anne Frank, is the personal diary of Annelies Marie Frank (1929–1945), a German-born Jewish girl who hid with her family in a concealed set of rooms (the Secret Annex, 'Achterhuis') in a warehouse at Prinsengracht 263 in Amsterdam from 6 July 1942 to 4 August 1944 — when they were discovered by the Gestapo and deported to Nazi concentration camps. Anne Frank wrote the diary between 12 June 1942 and 1 August 1944 in Dutch, initially in a red-and-white plaid autograph book, later in loose sheets; it was recovered from the Secret Annex after the arrest by Miep Gies (one of the helpers) and preserved. Anne died of typhus at Bergen-Belsen concentration camp in February or March 1945, weeks before the camp's liberation. Her father Otto Frank — the only member of the family to survive — had the diary published in 1947 as Het Achterhuis, translated into English in 1952, and subsequently into over 70 languages.

The Diary is one of the most widely read books in the world — over 35 million copies sold, translated into more than 70 languages — and the most widely read first-hand account of the Holocaust. Anne writes with remarkable intelligence, emotional depth, and literary self-awareness about life in hiding (the claustrophobia, the tensions, the fear, the daily routines), her developing inner life and intellectual ambitions, her first experience of love (with Peter van Pels), and her determined belief in human goodness despite the evidence around her — her famous last lines before arrest: 'I keep my ideals, because in spite of everything I still believe that people are really good at heart.' The combination of its intimate, personal voice, its historical testimony, and Anne's tragic fate have made the Diary one of the most powerful documents of the 20th century.

The Diary of Anne Frank has had enormous cultural impact — the Broadway play (1955, Pulitzer Prize) and film (1959) gave it a global audience; it has been a foundational text of Holocaust education in schools worldwide; and Anne Frank's face has become the most widely recognised symbol of the Holocaust's child victims — a humanising counterweight to the impersonal scale of six million deaths.","subjects":["Holocaust","Modern Era","World War II","Netherlands","Autobiography","Jewish History","20th Century","Holocaust Education"],"frameworks":["CAUSE_AND_EFFECT","STRUCTURAL_ANALYSIS"],"historicalSignificance":{"significanceScore":7,"significanceNarrative":"The Diary of Anne Frank is a testament to the resilience of human spirit in the face of unimaginable adversity, offering a powerful and poignant record of life under occupation.","significanceCategory":"regional"},"_editLog":[]}
